#
# CQ5 (INHABITED-RUNTIME-STACK.md §capability-use-versus-delegation): was a tool
# call made through a passive capability or delegated to another agent? Resolved
# WITHOUT a wrapper class: a gmeow:usedCapability edge from an invocation /
# execution to a logic:ActionSchema is PASSIVE use; a gmeow:ToolCall whose
# gmeow:usedTool points to a distinct gmeow:SoftwareAgent is DELEGATION. Over
# tool-usage.ttl this query returns the delegated tool agent alongside the
# passively-used capability schema — the structural discriminator, run over the
# merged ontology (asserted lane).
#
# The discriminator spans TWO extensions: gmeow:usedCapability is
# extensions/model-serving, gmeow:ToolCall / gmeow:usedTool are
# extensions/agentic, and neither may depend on the other (Principle 16). This
# PROFILE is where the question becomes legally askable, because a profile
# selects both and mints nothing — the same reason end-to-end.rq lives here
# rather than in the standalone model-serving slice.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
SELECT ?delegatedTool ?passiveCapability WHERE {
    ?toolCall a gmeow:ToolCall ;
        gmeow:usedTool ?delegatedTool .
    ?activity gmeow:usedCapability ?passiveCapability .
}
